erses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ"But ye have not so learned Christ;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWif so be that ye have heard him, and have been taught by him, as the truth is in Jesus:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrthat ye put off concerning the former conversation the old man, which is corrupt according to the deceitful lusts;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ*and be renewed in the spirit of your mind;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^and that ye put on the new man, which after God is created in righteousness and true holiness.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book0§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjWherefore putting away lying, speak every man truth with his neighbour: for we are members one of another.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book0§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBBe ye angry, and sin not: let not the sun go down upon your wrath:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ neither give place to the devil.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book0§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšLet him that stole steal no more: but rather let him labour, working with his hands the thing which is good, that he may have to give to him that needeth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book0§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Let no corrupt communication proceed out of your mouth, but that which is good to the use of edifying, that it may minister grace unto the hearers.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXAnd grieve not the holy Spirit of God, whereby ye are sealed unto the day of redemption.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book0§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpLet all bitterness, and wrath, and anger, and clamour, and evil speaking, be put away